/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 1 Kings chapters 16-20
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("1kings", [
{n:16, name:"Baasha to Ahab", seal:{ref:"1 Kings 16:33",verse:"And Ahab made a grove; and Ahab did more to provoke the LORD God of Israel to anger than all the kings of Israel that were before him."}, facts:["Did you know Zimri reigned only seven days, the shortest reign in the Bible's record of kings, and ended it by burning the palace down over himself (1 Kings 16:15-18)?","Did you know Omri bought the hill of Samaria from a man named Shemer for two talents of silver, and the city kept its former owner's name (1 Kings 16:24)?","Did you know Hiel the Bethelite rebuilt Jericho at the cost of his firstborn Abiram and his youngest Segub, exactly as Joshua had warned centuries before (1 Kings 16:34)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who brought the word of the LORD against Baasha?", options:["Jehu the son of Hanani","Ahijah the Shilonite","Shemaiah the man of God","Iddo the seer"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:1",verse:"Then the word of the LORD came to Jehu the son of Hanani against Baasha, saying,", insight:"God speaks against kings through prophets, not armies; His word is the true check on power."},
{q:"What had God done for Baasha before he sinned?", options:["Exalted him out of the dust and made him prince over Israel","Made him captain of the host","Given him the throne of David","Made him priest over the groves"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:2",verse:"Forasmuch as I exalted thee out of the dust, and made thee prince over my people Israel; and thou hast walked in the way of Jeroboam, and hast made my people Israel to sin, to provoke me to anger with their sins;", insight:"God reminds Baasha of grace before naming the sin; He shows us what He gave before He judges what we did."},
{q:"What did God say He would do to the house of Baasha?", options:["Take away its posterity and make it like the house of Jeroboam","Carry it captive to Assyria","Divide it between two kings","Set it over Judah"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:3",verse:"Behold, I will take away the posterity of Baasha, and the posterity of his house; and will make thy house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat.", insight:"Sin plants a harvest for the whole house; what a father sows in wickedness, his children reap in judgment."},
{q:"What would happen to those of Baasha's house who died in the city?", options:["The dogs would eat them","They would lie unburied in the streets","The lions would find them","They would be cast into the sea"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:4",verse:"Him that dieth of Baasha in the city shall the dogs eat; and him that dieth of his in the fields shall the fowls of the air eat.", insight:"A dishonored death was the sentence; God takes the body seriously, and how we end matters."},
{q:"Where was Baasha buried?", options:["In Tirzah","In Samaria","In Bethel","In Shechem"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:6",verse:"So Baasha slept with his fathers, and was buried in Tirzah: and Elah his son reigned in his stead.", insight:"Baasha was buried in Tirzah, but no tomb can hide a life from the record God keeps."},
{q:"In which year of Asa king of Judah did Elah begin to reign?", options:["The twenty and sixth year","The twenty and seventh year","The thirty and first year","The thirty and eighth year"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:8",verse:"In the twenty and sixth year of Asa king of Judah began Elah the son of Baasha to reign over Israel in Tirzah, two years.", insight:"Scripture dates the reigns of wicked kings with care; God keeps the calendar even when men ignore Him."},
{q:"How long did Elah reign over Israel?", options:["Two years","Seven days","Twelve years","Twenty and two years"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:8",verse:"In the twenty and sixth year of Asa king of Judah began Elah the son of Baasha to reign over Israel in Tirzah, two years.", insight:"Two years and gone; a throne built on sin is a short lease."},
{q:"Who conspired against Elah?", options:["Zimri, captain of half his chariots","Omri, captain of the host","Arza, steward of his house","Tibni, son of Ginath"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:9",verse:"And his servant Zimri, captain of half his chariots, conspired against him, as he was in Tirzah, drinking himself drunk in the house of Arza steward of his house in Tirzah.", insight:"The conspiracy came from inside the chariot corps; power gained by treachery is never safe from it."},
{q:"In whose house was Elah drinking himself drunk when Zimri struck?", options:["Arza, steward of his house, in Tirzah","Omri the captain, in Gibbethon","Baasha his father, in Samaria","Jehu the prophet, in Jezreel"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:9",verse:"And his servant Zimri, captain of half his chariots, conspired against him, as he was in Tirzah, drinking himself drunk in the house of Arza steward of his house in Tirzah.", insight:"Elah was drunk in a steward's house when death came; a king who cannot rule his appetites cannot rule a kingdom."},
{q:"In which year of Asa did Zimri slay Elah and reign in his stead?", options:["The twenty and seventh year","The twenty and sixth year","The thirty and first year","The thirty and eighth year"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:10",verse:"And Zimri went in and smote him, and killed him, in the twenty and seventh year of Asa king of Judah, and reigned in his stead.", insight:"Zimri's timing matched God's; even treachery serves the sentence God has already spoken."},
{q:"What was Zimri's first act as soon as he sat on the throne?", options:["He slew all the house of Baasha","He made peace with the Philistines","He built a house for Baal","He freed the captives of Judah"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:11",verse:"And it came to pass, when he began to reign, as soon as he sat on his throne, that he slew all the house of Baasha: he left him not one that pisseth against a wall, neither of his kinsfolks, nor of his friends.", insight:"Zimri wiped out Baasha's house completely; judgment that begins with God ends with nothing left."},
{q:"How long did Zimri reign in Tirzah?", options:["Seven days","Two years","Twelve years","Twenty and two years"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:15",verse:"In the twenty and seventh year of Asa king of Judah did Zimri reign seven days in Tirzah. And the people were encamped against Gibbethon, which belonged to the Philistines.", insight:"Seven days on the throne; the fastest fall in Israel's history warns that ill-gotten power burns out quickly."},
{q:"Where was Israel's army when Zimri seized the throne?", options:["Encamped against Gibbethon, which belonged to the Philistines","Encamped at Samaria","Marching on Ramoth-gilead","Gathered at the brook Kishon"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:15",verse:"In the twenty and seventh year of Asa king of Judah did Zimri reign seven days in Tirzah. And the people were encamped against Gibbethon, which belonged to the Philistines.", insight:"The army was away at Gibbethon while the capital fell; guard the heart, not just the borders."},
{q:"Whom did all Israel make king that day in the camp?", options:["Omri, the captain of the host","Tibni the son of Ginath","A brother of Zimri","The son of Elah"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:16",verse:"And the people that were encamped heard say, Zimri hath conspired, and hath also slain the king: wherefore all Israel made Omri, the captain of the host, king over Israel that day in the camp.", insight:"The camp chose Omri that very day; in crisis, men follow strength, but God weighs the heart."},
{q:"How did Zimri die when Omri took Tirzah?", options:["He burnt the king's house over himself with fire","He fell in battle at Gibbethon","He was slain by Omri's men","He fled to the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:18",verse:"And it came to pass, when Zimri saw that the city was taken, that he went into the palace of the king’s house, and burnt the king’s house over him with fire, and died,", insight:"Zimri died by his own fire; the violence we light often becomes our own end."},
{q:"After Zimri's death, how was Israel divided?", options:["Half followed Tibni the son of Ginath, and half followed Omri","Half went to Judah and half stayed in Israel","Half followed Zimri's son and half followed Omri","Half clung to Baasha's house and half followed Omri"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:21",verse:"Then were the people of Israel divided into two parts: half of the people followed Tibni the son of Ginath, to make him king; and half followed Omri.", insight:"A divided people chose two kings; division invites every ambitious man to claim the crown."},
{q:"From whom did Omri buy the hill of Samaria, and for how much?", options:["Shemer, for two talents of silver","The elders of Tirzah, for one talent of gold","The Philistines, for a hundred sheep","The king of Zidon, for cedar timber"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:24",verse:"And he bought the hill Samaria of Shemer for two talents of silver, and built on the hill, and called the name of the city which he built, after the name of Shemer, owner of the hill, Samaria.", insight:"Omri bought a hill and named it Samaria; empires rise on real estate, but only God gives a lasting city."},
{q:"In which year of Asa did Ahab begin to reign, and how long did he reign in Samaria?", options:["The thirty and eighth year; twenty and two years","The thirty and first year; twelve years","The twenty and seventh year; two years","The twenty and sixth year; seven days"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:29",verse:"And in the thirty and eighth year of Asa king of Judah began Ahab the son of Omri to reign over Israel: and Ahab the son of Omri reigned over Israel in Samaria twenty and two years.", insight:"Twenty-two years of Ahab began here; long reigns can be long judgments."},
{q:"How did Ahab's evil compare with the kings before him?", options:["He did evil above all that were before him","He did worse only than Jeroboam","He was milder than Baasha","He matched Omri but no more"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:30",verse:"And Ahab the son of Omri did evil in the sight of the LORD above all that were before him.", insight:"'Above all that were before him' is a terrible superlative; each generation can outdo the last in evil unless God intervenes."},
{q:"Whom did Ahab take to wife?", options:["Jezebel, daughter of Ethbaal king of the Zidonians","A daughter of Pharaoh","Maacah, daughter of Absalom","A daughter of the king of Moab"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 16:31",verse:"And it came to pass, as if it had been a light thing for him to walk in the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, that he took to wife Jezebel the daughter of Ethbaal king of the Zidonians, and went and served Baal, and worshipped him.", insight:"Ahab married into Baal worship; whom you yoke yourself to shapes whom you worship."}
]},
{n:17, name:"Elijah and the Drought", seal:{ref:"1 Kings 17:24",verse:"And the woman said to Elijah, Now by this I know that thou art a man of God, and that the word of the LORD in thy mouth is truth."}, facts:["Did you know God fed Elijah through ravens, birds the Law called unclean, bringing him bread and flesh twice a day at the brook Cherith (1 Kings 17:4-6)?","Did you know Zarephath belonged to Zidon, Jezebel's own homeland, so God sheltered His prophet in the very heart of Baal's country (1 Kings 17:9)?","Did you know Elijah stretched himself upon the widow's dead son three times, and the boy's soul came back into him, the first raising of the dead recorded in Scripture (1 Kings 17:21-22)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who was Elijah?", options:["The Tishbite, of the inhabitants of Gilead","A Levite of the sons of Aaron","A scribe from Jerusalem","A shepherd of Tekoa"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:1",verse:"And Elijah the Tishbite, who was of the inhabitants of Gilead, said unto Ahab, As the LORD God of Israel liveth, before whom I stand, there shall not be dew nor rain these years, but according to my word.", insight:"Elijah stood before the LORD before he stood before Ahab; hidden fellowship with God comes before public confrontation."},
{q:"What did Elijah declare to Ahab about dew and rain?", options:["There shall not be dew nor rain these years, but according to my word","There shall be rain in the third month","The drought shall last forty days","Rain shall fall only on Judah"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:1",verse:"And Elijah the Tishbite, who was of the inhabitants of Gilead, said unto Ahab, As the LORD God of Israel liveth, before whom I stand, there shall not be dew nor rain these years, but according to my word.", insight:"'But according to my word' shows the prophet carried God's authority; when God speaks through you, heaven backs the word."},
{q:"Where did God tell Elijah to hide himself?", options:["By the brook Cherith, that is before Jordan","In a cave on Mount Carmel","In the wilderness of Beer-sheba","In the hills of Ephraim"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:3",verse:"Get thee hence, and turn thee eastward, and hide thyself by the brook Cherith, that is before Jordan.", insight:"God hid His prophet before He used him; obscurity is often God's classroom for the bold."},
{q:"Whom did God command to feed Elijah at Cherith?", options:["The ravens","The doves of the valley","The priests of Gilead","The merchants of Jordan"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:4",verse:"And it shall be, that thou shalt drink of the brook; and I have commanded the ravens to feed thee there.", insight:"God commanded ravens, unclean birds, to feed His servant; He can make any creature serve His saints."},
{q:"What did the ravens bring Elijah, and when?", options:["Bread and flesh in the morning, and bread and flesh in the evening","Manna at sunrise and quails at dusk","Fish from Jordan at noon","Grain from the threshing floor"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:6",verse:"And the ravens brought him bread and flesh in the morning, and bread and flesh in the evening; and he drank of the brook.", insight:"Bread and flesh morning and evening, like manna on schedule; God's provision keeps appointments."},
{q:"Why did the brook Cherith dry up?", options:["Because there had been no rain in the land","Because the Syrians dammed it","Because the ravens fouled it","Because an earthquake split it"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:7",verse:"And it came to pass after a while, that the brook dried up, because there had been no rain in the land.", insight:"Even the brook God provided ran dry; when the first supply fails, God is only moving you to the next."},
{q:"To what city did God send Elijah after Cherith?", options:["Zarephath, which belongeth to Zidon","Tyre, on the coast","Damascus, in Syria","Ekron, of the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:9",verse:"Arise, get thee to Zarephath, which belongeth to Zidon, and dwell there: behold, I have commanded a widow woman there to sustain thee.", insight:"God sent Elijah to Zarephath of Zidon, Jezebel's country; grace goes looking for the unlikely, in the unlikeliest places."},
{q:"Whom had God commanded to sustain Elijah at Zarephath?", options:["A widow woman","A wealthy merchant","The governor of the city","A priest of Baal"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:9",verse:"Arise, get thee to Zarephath, which belongeth to Zidon, and dwell there: behold, I have commanded a widow woman there to sustain thee.", insight:"A widow, the poorest provider, was chosen to sustain the prophet; God delights to use the overlooked."},
{q:"Where did Elijah meet the widow, and what was she doing?", options:["At the gate of the city, gathering sticks","At the well, drawing water","In the marketplace, buying meal","At the city wall, begging bread"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:10",verse:"So he arose and went to Zarephath. And when he came to the gate of the city, behold, the widow woman was there gathering of sticks: and he called to her, and said, Fetch me, I pray thee, a little water in a vessel, that I may drink.", insight:"She was gathering sticks, preparing her last meal; God often meets us at the very end of our resources."},
{q:"What did Elijah first ask the widow to fetch him?", options:["A little water in a vessel, that he might drink","A bed in her house","A cloak for the night","A guide to the city"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:10",verse:"So he arose and went to Zarephath. And when he came to the gate of the city, behold, the widow woman was there gathering of sticks: and he called to her, and said, Fetch me, I pray thee, a little water in a vessel, that I may drink.", insight:"He asked for water first; small requests of faith open the door to greater miracles."},
{q:"What did the widow say she had left in the house?", options:["A handful of meal in a barrel, and a little oil in a cruse","Two loaves and a skin of wine","A basket of figs and a jar of honey","Nothing at all"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:12",verse:"And she said, As the LORD thy God liveth, I have not a cake, but an handful of meal in a barrel, and a little oil in a cruse: and, behold, I am gathering two sticks, that I may go in and dress it for me and my son, that we may eat it, and die.", insight:"A handful of meal and a little oil, honestly confessed; bring God what you have, even when it is almost nothing."},
{q:"What did the widow say she would do with her last meal?", options:["Dress it for herself and her son, that they might eat it and die","Offer it at the altar of Baal","Sell it to pay her debts","Hide it from the tax collectors"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:12",verse:"And she said, As the LORD thy God liveth, I have not a cake, but an handful of meal in a barrel, and a little oil in a cruse: and, behold, I am gathering two sticks, that I may go in and dress it for me and my son, that we may eat it, and die.", insight:"'That we may eat it, and die' was her honest despair; God heard it and answered with life."},
{q:"What did Elijah tell the widow to make first?", options:["A little cake for him first, then for herself and her son","A sacrifice for the LORD","Bread for the whole city","A double portion for the morrow"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:13",verse:"And Elijah said unto her, Fear not; go and do as thou hast said: but make me thereof a little cake first, and bring it unto me, and after make for thee and for thy son.", insight:"The prophet's portion came first; putting God first is the doorway through which provision flows."},
{q:"What did Elijah promise about the meal and the oil?", options:["The barrel of meal shall not waste, neither shall the cruse of oil fail, until the LORD sendeth rain","They would double every morning","They would feed the whole city","They would last until the feast of harvest"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:14",verse:"For thus saith the LORD God of Israel, The barrel of meal shall not waste, neither shall the cruse of oil fail, until the day that the LORD sendeth rain upon the earth.", insight:"'Shall not waste, shall not fail' until the rain; God's promises carry a term of His choosing, not ours."},
{q:"What happened when the widow obeyed Elijah?", options:["She, and he, and her house, did eat many days","The meal ran out that night","The neighbors took her food","Ahab's men seized the barrel"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:15",verse:"And she went and did according to the saying of Elijah: and she, and he, and her house, did eat many days.", insight:"She obeyed and ate many days; obedience turned a last meal into a lasting supply."},
{q:"What happened to the widow's son?", options:["He fell sick, and there was no breath left in him","He ran away to Zidon","He was taken by Ahab's soldiers","He fell into the brook"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:17",verse:"And it came to pass after these things, that the son of the woman, the mistress of the house, fell sick; and his sickness was so sore, that there was no breath left in him.", insight:"Sorrow followed blessing; even in the house of miracles, death knocked."},
{q:"What did the widow say to Elijah over her dead son?", options:["Art thou come to call my sin to remembrance, and to slay my son?","Take thy God and leave my house","Why didst thou eat my bread?","Send me to another prophet"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:18",verse:"And she said unto Elijah, What have I to do with thee, O thou man of God? art thou come unto me to call my sin to remembrance, and to slay my son?", insight:"Grief accused the prophet; pain often questions the very grace that sustains it."},
{q:"Where did Elijah lay the dead child?", options:["He carried him to a loft and laid him upon his own bed","He laid him at the city gate","He buried him outside the walls","He left him in his mother's arms"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:19",verse:"And he said unto her, Give me thy son. And he took him out of her bosom, and carried him up into a loft, where he abode, and laid him upon his own bed.", insight:"Elijah carried the boy to his own bed; true intercession takes the burden close and personal."},
{q:"How many times did Elijah stretch himself upon the child?", options:["Three times","Once","Seven times","Forty times"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:21",verse:"And he stretched himself upon the child three times, and cried unto the LORD, and said, O LORD my God, I pray thee, let this child’s soul come into him again.", insight:"Three times he stretched himself out; persistent prayer does not quit after the first asking."},
{q:"What happened when the LORD heard Elijah's voice?", options:["The soul of the child came into him again, and he revived","Fire fell from heaven","The house shook","A voice answered from the cloud"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 17:22",verse:"And the LORD heard the voice of Elijah; and the soul of the child came into him again, and he revived.", insight:"The LORD heard the voice of Elijah; heaven still answers the cries of those who stand before Him."}
]},
{n:18, name:"Fire on Mount Carmel", seal:{ref:"1 Kings 18:39",verse:"And when all the people saw it, they fell on their faces: and they said, The LORD, he is the God; the LORD, he is the God."}, facts:["Did you know Obadiah hid a hundred prophets of the LORD in caves and fed them with bread and water while managing the household of Ahab, the king hunting them (1 Kings 18:3-4)?","Did you know Elijah ordered four barrels of water poured over his sacrifice three times, soaking wood, altar, and trench, so no one could credit the fire to any trick (1 Kings 18:33-35)?","Did you know the first sign of rain was only a little cloud like a man's hand, yet Elijah ran on foot ahead of Ahab's chariot all the way to Jezreel (1 Kings 18:44-46)?"], questions:[
{q:"In which year did the LORD send Elijah to show himself to Ahab, and what did He promise?", options:["In the third year; I will send rain upon the earth","In the first year; I will smite Baal","In the seventh year; I will judge Jezebel","In the fortieth year; I will restore Israel"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:1",verse:"And it came to pass after many days, that the word of the LORD came to Elijah in the third year, saying, Go, shew thyself unto Ahab; and I will send rain upon the earth.", insight:"In the third year God said, 'I will send rain'; judgment has a set term, and mercy has a set time."},
{q:"Who was Obadiah?", options:["The governor of Ahab's house, who feared the LORD greatly","A captain of Ahab's chariots","A prophet of Baal turned to the LORD","The steward of Jezebel's table"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:3",verse:"And Ahab called Obadiah, which was the governor of his house. (Now Obadiah feared the LORD greatly:", insight:"Obadiah feared the LORD greatly while serving Ahab; you can keep a clean conscience in a corrupt court."},
{q:"What had Obadiah done when Jezebel cut off the prophets of the LORD?", options:["Hid a hundred prophets by fifty in a cave, and fed them with bread and water","Fled with them to Judah","Bribed the soldiers to spare them","Sent them to Elijah at Cherith"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:4",verse:"For it was so, when Jezebel cut off the prophets of the LORD, that Obadiah took an hundred prophets, and hid them by fifty in a cave, and fed them with bread and water.)", insight:"He hid a hundred prophets at his own risk; quiet courage feeds the faithful when the powerful hunt them."},
{q:"What message did Elijah send to Ahab by Obadiah?", options:["Go, tell thy lord, Behold, Elijah is here","Tell thy lord to repent or die","Tell thy lord the drought is ended","Tell thy lord to meet me at Jezreel"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:8",verse:"And he answered him, I am: go, tell thy lord, Behold, Elijah is here.", insight:"'Behold, Elijah is here' was a dangerous message; carrying God's word sometimes costs the carrier."},
{q:"How far had Ahab's search for Elijah gone?", options:["There was no nation or kingdom where he had not sent, and he took an oath they had not found him","He searched only Israel","He sent to Egypt alone","He never searched at all"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:10",verse:"As the LORD thy God liveth, there is no nation or kingdom, whither my lord hath not sent to seek thee: and when they said, He is not there; he took an oath of the kingdom and nation, that they found thee not.", insight:"Ahab searched every nation for Elijah; the world hunts God's messengers but cannot find them until God says go."},
{q:"What oath did Elijah swear to Obadiah?", options:["As the LORD of hosts liveth, I will surely show myself unto him today","By the altar of Carmel I will not flee","By the drought itself I will appear","By the prophets hidden in the cave"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:15",verse:"And Elijah said, As the LORD of hosts liveth, before whom I stand, I will surely shew myself unto him to day.", insight:"Elijah swore by the living LORD; certainty about God steadies you before kings."},
{q:"What did Ahab call Elijah when they met?", options:["Art thou he that troubleth Israel?","My lord the prophet","The man of God","The Tishbite"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:17",verse:"And it came to pass, when Ahab saw Elijah, that Ahab said unto him, Art thou he that troubleth Israel?", insight:"'Art thou he that troubleth Israel?' The guilty always blame the prophet for the trouble their sin caused."},
{q:"How did Elijah answer Ahab's charge?", options:["I have not troubled Israel; but thou and thy father's house have forsaken the commandments of the LORD","I trouble no one; I only pray","The drought troubles Israel, not I","Thy prophets trouble thee, not I"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:18",verse:"And he answered, I have not troubled Israel; but thou, and thy father’s house, in that ye have forsaken the commandments of the LORD, and thou hast followed Baalim.", insight:"Elijah named the real troublers: those who forsook God's commandments; sin troubles a nation, not the one who exposes it."},
{q:"How many prophets of Baal were to gather at Mount Carmel?", options:["Four hundred and fifty","Four hundred","One hundred","Fifty"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:19",verse:"Now therefore send, and gather to me all Israel unto mount Carmel, and the prophets of Baal four hundred and fifty, and the prophets of the groves four hundred, which eat at Jezebel’s table.", insight:"Four hundred and fifty against one; God's arithmetic is not ours."},
{q:"How many prophets of the groves were there, and whose table did they eat at?", options:["Four hundred, which eat at Jezebel's table","Four hundred and fifty, which eat at Ahab's table","One hundred, which eat at Obadiah's table","Fifty, which eat at the king's gate"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:19",verse:"Now therefore send, and gather to me all Israel unto mount Carmel, and the prophets of Baal four hundred and fifty, and the prophets of the groves four hundred, which eat at Jezebel’s table.", insight:"They ate at Jezebel's table; false prophets are fed by the powers that use them."},
{q:"What challenge did Elijah set before all the people?", options:["How long halt ye between two opinions? If the LORD be God, follow him; but if Baal, then follow him","Choose this day whom ye will serve","Return to the LORD or perish","Bring your sacrifices to Carmel"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:21",verse:"And Elijah came unto all the people, and said, How long halt ye between two opinions? if the LORD be God, follow him: but if Baal, then follow him. And the people answered him not a word.", insight:"'How long halt ye between two opinions?' God will not share your heart with an idol."},
{q:"What test would decide between the LORD and Baal?", options:["The God that answereth by fire, let him be God","The god whose priests fast longest","The god whose altar stands highest","The god whose prophets sing loudest"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:24",verse:"And call ye on the name of your gods, and I will call on the name of the LORD: and the God that answereth by fire, let him be God. And all the people answered and said, It is well spoken.", insight:"The God that answers by fire; true religion is proven by a God who actually answers."},
{q:"How did Elijah mock Baal's prophets at noon?", options:["Cry aloud, for he is talking, or pursuing, or on a journey, or sleepeth","Dance harder, for he loves the dance","Offer more, for he is hungry","Be silent, for he is resting"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:27",verse:"And it came to pass at noon, that Elijah mocked them, and said, Cry aloud: for he is a god; either he is talking, or he is pursuing, or he is in a journey, or peradventure he sleepeth, and must be awaked.", insight:"Elijah mocked the idol's silence; idols deserve ridicule, not reverence."},
{q:"What did Baal's prophets do to themselves?", options:["Cut themselves with knives and lancets till the blood gushed out","Tore their clothes and fasted","Lay prostrate till evening","Beat their breasts with stones"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:28",verse:"And they cried aloud, and cut themselves after their manner with knives and lancets, till the blood gushed out upon them.", insight:"They cut themselves till blood gushed, and nothing answered; self-harm never moves a god who does not exist."},
{q:"How many stones did Elijah use for the altar, and why?", options:["Twelve, according to the number of the tribes of the sons of Jacob","Seven, for the days of creation","Ten, for the commandments","Forty, for the years in the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:31",verse:"And Elijah took twelve stones, according to the number of the tribes of the sons of Jacob, unto whom the word of the LORD came, saying, Israel shall be thy name:", insight:"Twelve stones for twelve tribes; true worship remembers the whole people of God."},
{q:"How much water did Elijah have poured on the sacrifice?", options:["Four barrels, poured three times","One barrel, poured once","Seven barrels, poured seven times","Twelve barrels, poured twelve times"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:34",verse:"And he said, Do it the second time. And they did it the second time. And he said, Do it the third time. And they did it the third time.", insight:"Three soakings of water removed every excuse; faith does not fear making the miracle harder."},
{q:"How did Elijah address God when he prayed?", options:["LORD God of Abraham, Isaac, and of Israel","O Thou that dwellest in heaven","God of the thunder and the fire","LORD of hosts, King of glory"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:36",verse:"And it came to pass at the time of the offering of the evening sacrifice, that Elijah the prophet came near, and said, LORD God of Abraham, Isaac, and of Israel, let it be known this day that thou art God in Israel, and that I am thy servant, and that I have done all these things at thy word.", insight:"Elijah prayed to the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Israel; he anchored his prayer in covenant history."},
{q:"What did the fire of the LORD consume?", options:["The burnt sacrifice, the wood, the stones, the dust, and it licked up the water in the trench","Only the bullock on the altar","The prophets of Baal","The whole top of Carmel"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:38",verse:"Then the fire of the LORD fell, and consumed the burnt sacrifice, and the wood, and the stones, and the dust, and licked up the water that was in the trench.", insight:"The fire licked up even the water; when God answers, He answers completely."},
{q:"What did the people cry when they saw the fire fall?", options:["The LORD, he is the God; the LORD, he is the God","Great is Baal of the heavens","Elijah is the prophet of the LORD","Holy, holy, holy is His name"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:39",verse:"And when all the people saw it, they fell on their faces: and they said, The LORD, he is the God; the LORD, he is the God.", insight:"The people fell on their faces in confession; seeing God's power should end in worship, not applause."},
{q:"What became of the prophets of Baal?", options:["Elijah brought them down to the brook Kishon and slew them there","They fled to Zidon","They repented and worshipped the LORD","Ahab pardoned them"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 18:40",verse:"And Elijah said unto them, Take the prophets of Baal; let not one of them escape. And they took them: and Elijah brought them down to the brook Kishon, and slew them there.", insight:"The false prophets were judged at Kishon; God will not let lies stand beside His altar forever."}
]},
{n:19, name:"The Still Small Voice", seal:{ref:"1 Kings 19:12",verse:"And after the earthquake a fire; but the LORD was not in the fire: and after the fire a still small voice."}, facts:["Did you know the LORD passed by Horeb in a wind that tore the mountains, then an earthquake, then fire, and was in none of them, speaking instead in a still small voice (1 Kings 19:11-12)?","Did you know that when Elijah said 'I, even I only, am left,' God answered that seven thousand in Israel had never bowed the knee to Baal (1 Kings 19:10, 19:18)?","Did you know Elisha burned his farming tools to cook his farewell feast, turning his plow into firewood so there was no going back (1 Kings 19:21)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did Ahab report to Jezebel?", options:["All that Elijah had done, and how he had slain all the prophets with the sword","That Elijah had fled to Judah","That the drought was ended","That Baal's prophets had won"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:1",verse:"And Ahab told Jezebel all that Elijah had done, and withal how he had slain all the prophets with the sword.", insight:"Ahab told Jezebel everything; victories must be guarded, because the enemy hears the report too."},
{q:"What did Jezebel swear to do to Elijah?", options:["Make his life as the life of one of the slain prophets by tomorrow","Burn him on Mount Carmel","Cast him into prison","Send him to Zidon in chains"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:2",verse:"Then Jezebel sent a messenger unto Elijah, saying, So let the gods do to me, and more also, if I make not thy life as the life of one of them by to morrow about this time.", insight:"One threat undid the man of Carmel; even giants of faith can fall the day after the triumph."},
{q:"Where did Elijah flee, and whom did he leave there?", options:["To Beer-sheba, which belongeth to Judah; he left his servant there","To Damascus; he left his mantle there","To Egypt; he left his staff there","To Moab; he left his provisions there"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:3",verse:"And when he saw that, he arose, and went for his life, and came to Beer-sheba, which belongeth to Judah, and left his servant there.", insight:"He fled to Beer-sheba and left his servant; exhaustion makes us run and isolates us."},
{q:"Where did Elijah sit in the wilderness, and what did he ask God?", options:["Under a juniper tree; he asked God to take away his life, for he was not better than his fathers","Under an oak; he asked for bread","By a brook; he asked for water","On a rock; he asked for strength"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:4",verse:"But he himself went a day’s journey into the wilderness, and came and sat down under a juniper tree: and he requested for himself that he might die; and said, It is enough; now, O LORD, take away my life; for I am not better than my fathers.", insight:"Under the juniper he asked to die; God does not rebuke honest despair, He feeds it."},
{q:"What did the angel say when he first touched Elijah?", options:["Arise and eat","Fear not, for I am with thee","Return to Samaria","Sleep, for thou art weary"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:5",verse:"And as he lay and slept under a juniper tree, behold, then an angel touched him, and said unto him, Arise and eat.", insight:"'Arise and eat' was God's first medicine; sometimes grace comes as a meal and rest before it comes as a word."},
{q:"What did Elijah find at his head when he woke?", options:["A cake baken on the coals, and a cruse of water","Manna and quails","Bread and wine","Figs and honey"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:6",verse:"And he looked, and, behold, there was a cake baken on the coals, and a cruse of water at his head. And he did eat and drink, and laid him down again.", insight:"A cake on the coals and water at his head; God tends to broken servants with simple, tangible care."},
{q:"Why did the angel wake Elijah a second time to eat?", options:["Because the journey was too great for him","Because the food would spoil","Because the sun was rising","Because Jezebel's men were near"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:7",verse:"And the angel of the LORD came again the second time, and touched him, and said, Arise and eat; because the journey is too great for thee.", insight:"'The journey is too great for thee'; God knows our limits better than we do and provides for the road ahead."},
{q:"How long did that meal sustain Elijah, and where did he go?", options:["Forty days and forty nights, unto Horeb the mount of God","Seven days, unto Beer-sheba","Three days, unto Damascus","One year, unto Zarephath"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:8",verse:"And he arose, and did eat and drink, and went in the strength of that meat forty days and forty nights unto Horeb the mount of God.", insight:"Forty days on one meal to Horeb; God's strength outlasts our weakness."},
{q:"What question greeted Elijah at the cave?", options:["What doest thou here, Elijah?","Wherefore hast thou fled?","Who sent thee hither?","How long wilt thou hide?"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:9",verse:"And he came thither unto a cave, and lodged there; and, behold, the word of the LORD came to him, and he said unto him, What doest thou here, Elijah?", insight:"'What doest thou here, Elijah?' God asks the question that makes us examine our running."},
{q:"What was Elijah's complaint to the LORD?", options:["Israel had forsaken the covenant, thrown down the altars, and slain the prophets, and he alone was left","Jezebel had taken the throne","Ahab had joined with Syria","The drought had never ended"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:10",verse:"And he said, I have been very jealous for the LORD God of hosts: for the children of Israel have forsaken thy covenant, thrown down thine altars, and slain thy prophets with the sword; and I, even I only, am left; and they seek my life, to take it away.", insight:"Elijah's complaint was partly true and partly blind; discouragement edits out the seven thousand."},
{q:"What did the great and strong wind do, and was the LORD in it?", options:["It rent the mountains and brake the rocks, but the LORD was not in the wind","It carried Elijah to heaven, for the LORD was in it","It scattered the altar stones, and the LORD judged by it","It dried the brook, and the LORD spoke in it"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:11",verse:"And he said, Go forth, and stand upon the mount before the LORD. And, behold, the LORD passed by, and a great and strong wind rent the mountains, and brake in pieces the rocks before the LORD; but the LORD was not in the wind: and after the wind an earthquake; but the LORD was not in the earthquake:", insight:"The wind tore the mountains, but the LORD was not in it; God's greatest works are not always His loudest."},
{q:"What came after the fire?", options:["A still small voice","A mighty thunder","A second earthquake","A pillar of cloud"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:12",verse:"And after the earthquake a fire; but the LORD was not in the fire: and after the fire a still small voice.", insight:"After the fire, a still small voice; God often whispers what the storm cannot say."},
{q:"What did Elijah do when he heard the voice?", options:["He wrapped his face in his mantle and stood in the entering in of the cave","He fell on his face on the ground","He ran out to meet the LORD","He built an altar at the cave mouth"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:13",verse:"And it was so, when Elijah heard it, that he wrapped his face in his mantle, and went out, and stood in the entering in of the cave. And, behold, there came a voice unto him, and said, What doest thou here, Elijah?", insight:"He wrapped his face in his mantle; reverence covers the face before glory speaks."},
{q:"Where was Elijah told to go, and whom was he to anoint?", options:["Return to the wilderness of Damascus, and anoint Hazael king over Syria","Go to Samaria, and anoint Ahab's son","Flee to Egypt, and anoint Pharaoh","Return to Gilead, and anoint a prophet"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:15",verse:"And the LORD said unto him, Go, return on thy way to the wilderness of Damascus: and when thou comest, anoint Hazael to be king over Syria:", insight:"God sent him back the way he came, with work to do; the cure for despair is a commission."},
{q:"Whom was Elijah to anoint king over Israel?", options:["Jehu the son of Nimshi","Elisha the son of Shaphat","Hazael of Syria","Obadiah the governor"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:16",verse:"And Jehu the son of Nimshi shalt thou anoint to be king over Israel: and Elisha the son of Shaphat of Abel-meholah shalt thou anoint to be prophet in thy room.", insight:"Jehu would be king, judgment with a sword; God raises instruments of justice in His own time."},
{q:"Who was to be prophet in Elijah's room?", options:["Elisha the son of Shaphat of Abel-meholah","Obadiah the governor","The son of the widow of Zarephath","A son of the prophets"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:16",verse:"And Jehu the son of Nimshi shalt thou anoint to be king over Israel: and Elisha the son of Shaphat of Abel-meholah shalt thou anoint to be prophet in thy room.", insight:"Elisha would be prophet in his room; no servant of God is irreplaceable, and succession is God's plan."},
{q:"How many in Israel had God reserved who never bowed to Baal?", options:["Seven thousand","One hundred","Forty thousand","Twelve thousand"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:18",verse:"Yet I have left me seven thousand in Israel, all the knees which have not bowed unto Baal, and every mouth which hath not kissed him.", insight:"Seven thousand knees never bowed; you are never as alone as despair tells you."},
{q:"What was Elisha doing when Elijah found him?", options:["Plowing with twelve yoke of oxen before him, and he with the twelfth","Keeping sheep in Abel-meholah","Drawing water at the well","Sitting at the city gate"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:19",verse:"So he departed thence, and found Elisha the son of Shaphat, who was plowing with twelve yoke of oxen before him, and he with the twelfth: and Elijah passed by him, and cast his mantle upon him.", insight:"Elisha was plowing with twelve yoke when called; God calls busy hands, not idle ones."},
{q:"What did Elijah do to Elisha as he passed by?", options:["He cast his mantle upon him","He anointed his head with oil","He laid his hands on him","He gave him his staff"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:19",verse:"So he departed thence, and found Elisha the son of Shaphat, who was plowing with twelve yoke of oxen before him, and he with the twelfth: and Elijah passed by him, and cast his mantle upon him.", insight:"The mantle fell on him as Elijah passed by; calling often comes suddenly, in the middle of ordinary work."},
{q:"What did Elisha ask before following Elijah?", options:["Let me kiss my father and my mother, and then I will follow thee","Give me a double portion of thy spirit","Let me finish the plowing first","Suffer me to bury my father"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 19:20",verse:"And he left the oxen, and ran after Elijah, and said, Let me, I pray thee, kiss my father and my mother, and then I will follow thee. And he said unto him, Go back again: for what have I done to thee?", insight:"He asked to kiss his parents farewell; honoring family and following God belong together."}
]},
{n:20, name:"Ahab and Ben-hadad", seal:{ref:"1 Kings 20:28",verse:"And there came a man of God, and spake unto the king of Israel, and said, Thus saith the LORD, Because the Syrians have said, The LORD is God of the hills, but he is not God of the valleys, therefore will I deliver all this great multitude into thine hand, and ye shall know that I am the LORD."}, facts:["Did you know Israel's army at Aphek numbered only seven thousand men, looking like 'two little flocks of kids' against Syrians who filled the country, yet they won, and a falling wall finished twenty-seven thousand more (1 Kings 20:15, 20:27, 20:30)?","Did you know the Syrians believed the LORD was only a God of the hills, so they fought in the plain at Aphek, and the LORD beat them there to prove them wrong (1 Kings 20:23, 20:28)?","Did you know Ahab called Ben-hadad 'my brother,' made a covenant with him, and let him go, for which the LORD said Ahab's life would go for his (1 Kings 20:32-34, 20:42)?"], questions:[
{q:"How many kings came with Ben-hadad to besiege Samaria?", options:["Thirty and two","Twelve","Seven","Fifty"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:1",verse:"And Ben-hadad the king of Syria gathered all his host together: and there were thirty and two kings with him, and horses, and chariots: and he went up and besieged Samaria, and warred against it.", insight:"Thirty-two kings against one city; the odds look worst right before God shows His hand."},
{q:"What did Ben-hadad claim as his own?", options:["Israel's silver and gold, wives and children, even the goodliest","The walls and gates of Samaria","The temple vessels and the palace","The horses, chariots, and armor"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:3",verse:"Thy silver and thy gold is mine; thy wives also and thy children, even the goodliest, are mine.", insight:"Ben-hadad claimed everything, even the goodliest; bullies always overreach."},
{q:"How did Ahab first answer Ben-hadad?", options:["I am thine, and all that I have","Come and take them if thou canst","I will meet thee at noon","The elders forbid it"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:4",verse:"And the king of Israel answered and said, My lord, O king, according to thy saying, I am thine, and all that I have.", insight:"Ahab surrendered everything at first; fear gives away what faith would defend."},
{q:"What did the elders and all the people counsel Ahab?", options:["Hearken not unto him, nor consent","Pay him double","Flee to Judah","Offer him thy daughters"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:8",verse:"And all the elders and all the people said unto him, Hearken not unto him, nor consent.", insight:"The elders said, 'Hearken not'; wise counsel stiffens the spine when tyrants demand more."},
{q:"What proverb did Ahab send back to Ben-hadad's boast?", options:["Let not him that girdeth on his harness boast himself as he that putteth it off","The race is not to the swift","Pride goeth before a fall","A soft answer turneth away wrath"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:11",verse:"And the king of Israel answered and said, Tell him, Let not him that girdeth on his harness boast himself as he that putteth it off.", insight:"Do not boast before the battle; God loves to humble the loudmouth."},
{q:"What was Ben-hadad doing when the battle began?", options:["Drinking himself drunk in the pavilions with the kings","Sacrificing to his gods","Reviewing his chariots","Writing to Damascus"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:12",verse:"And it came to pass, when Ben-hadad heard this message, as he was drinking, he and the kings in the pavilions, that he said unto his servants, Set yourselves in array. And they set themselves in array against the city.", insight:"Ben-hadad was drinking when war came; arrogance parties while danger marches."},
{q:"What did the prophet promise Ahab?", options:["I will deliver this multitude into thine hand this day, and thou shalt know that I am the LORD","Flee, for Samaria shall fall","Make peace, for thou canst not win","The Syrians shall serve thee"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:13",verse:"And, behold, there came a prophet unto Ahab king of Israel, saying, Thus saith the LORD, Hast thou seen all this great multitude? behold, I will deliver it into thine hand this day; and thou shalt know that I am the LORD.", insight:"God promised deliverance 'that thou shalt know that I am the LORD'; even an unworthy king gets a lesson in who God is."},
{q:"By whom did the LORD say He would deliver the Syrians?", options:["Even by the young men of the princes of the provinces","By the elders of Israel","By the captains of Judah","By the sons of the prophets"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:14",verse:"And Ahab said, By whom? And he said, Thus saith the LORD, Even by the young men of the princes of the provinces. Then he said, Who shall order the battle? And he answered, Thou.", insight:"Victory would come by the young men of the princes; God uses the unlikely to shame the mighty."},
{q:"How many young men of the princes of the provinces were numbered?", options:["Two hundred and thirty two","Thirty and two","Seven thousand","One hundred"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:15",verse:"Then he numbered the young men of the princes of the provinces, and they were two hundred and thirty two: and after them he numbered all the people, even all the children of Israel, being seven thousand.", insight:"Two hundred and thirty-two against thirty-two kings; God's math embarrasses the world's."},
{q:"At what time did Israel go out to battle?", options:["At noon","At midnight","At dawn","At the evening sacrifice"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:16",verse:"And they went out at noon. But Ben-hadad was drinking himself drunk in the pavilions, he and the kings, the thirty and two kings that helped him.", insight:"Israel went out at noon while Ben-hadad drank; discipline beats indulgence."},
{q:"What were Ben-hadad's orders about the men coming out of Samaria?", options:["Take them alive, whether they come for peace or for war","Slay every man","Let them pass unharmed","Bring them for ransom"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:18",verse:"And he said, Whether they be come out for peace, take them alive; or whether they be come out for war, take them alive.", insight:"'Take them alive' was his order; pride assumed a victory it never fought for."},
{q:"What warning did the prophet give Ahab after the victory?", options:["At the return of the year the king of Syria will come up against thee","Ben-hadad is dead","Syria will sue for peace","Go up now and take Damascus"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:22",verse:"And the prophet came to the king of Israel, and said unto him, Go, strengthen thyself, and mark, and see what thou doest: for at the return of the year the king of Syria will come up against thee.", insight:"The prophet warned of next year's war; one victory is not the end of the battle, so stay ready."},
{q:"Why did the Syrians want to fight Israel in the plain?", options:["They said Israel's God was a God of the hills only","Their chariots needed flat ground","Their horses feared the heights","The plains had more water"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:23",verse:"And the servants of the king of Syria said unto him, Their gods are gods of the hills; therefore they were stronger than we; but let us fight against them in the plain, and surely we shall be stronger than they.", insight:"They called Him a God of the hills only; small views of God lead to big mistakes."},
{q:"How did Israel's army look beside Syria's at Aphek?", options:["Like two little flocks of kids, while the Syrians filled the country","Like locusts covering the hills","Like stars without number","Like sand on the seashore"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:27",verse:"And the children of Israel were numbered, and were all present, and went against them: and the children of Israel pitched before them like two little flocks of kids; but the Syrians filled the country.", insight:"Two little flocks of kids against an army that filled the country; God defends the outnumbered."},
{q:"Why did the LORD promise to deliver the multitude at Aphek?", options:["Because Syria said the LORD was God of the hills but not of the valleys","Because Ahab had repented","Because the prophets had prayed","Because Israel was innocent"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:28",verse:"And there came a man of God, and spake unto the king of Israel, and said, Thus saith the LORD, Because the Syrians have said, The LORD is God of the hills, but he is not God of the valleys, therefore will I deliver all this great multitude into thine hand, and ye shall know that I am the LORD.", insight:"God would not be boxed into the hills; He is Lord of valleys too, and of every place men limit Him."},
{q:"How many Syrian footmen did Israel slay in one day?", options:["An hundred thousand","Twenty and seven thousand","Seven thousand","Two hundred and thirty two"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:29",verse:"And they pitched one over against the other seven days. And so it was, that in the seventh day the battle was joined: and the children of Israel slew of the Syrians an hundred thousand footmen in one day.", insight:"A hundred thousand fell in one day; when God fights, the numbers are His."},
{q:"In what dress did Ben-hadad's servants come to Ahab?", options:["Sackcloth on their loins, and ropes upon their heads","Armor and helmets","White robes of peace","Chains of iron"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:31",verse:"And his servants said unto him, Behold now, we have heard that the kings of the house of Israel are merciful kings: let us, I pray thee, put sackcloth on our loins, and ropes upon our heads, and go out to the king of Israel: peradventure he will save thy life.", insight:"They came in sackcloth with ropes; humility, even from enemies, opens the door to mercy."},
{q:"What did Ahab say when he heard Ben-hadad was alive?", options:["Is he yet alive? He is my brother","Bring him bound in chains","Let him die in the inner chamber","Sell him for a talent of silver"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:32",verse:"So they girded sackcloth on their loins, and put ropes on their heads, and came to the king of Israel, and said, Thy servant Ben-hadad saith, I pray thee, let me live. And he said, Is he yet alive? he is my brother.", insight:"'He is my brother,' said Ahab; misplaced kindness to God's enemy is cruelty to God's people."},
{q:"What did Ahab do with Ben-hadad instead of destroying him?", options:["He made a covenant with him and sent him away","He slew him at Aphek","He put him in prison","He made him his servant"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:34",verse:"And Ben-hadad said unto him, The cities, which my father took from thy father, I will restore; and thou shalt make streets for thee in Damascus, as my father made in Samaria. Then said Ahab, I will send thee away with this covenant. So he made a covenant with him, and sent him away.", insight:"Ahab made a covenant and let him go; disobedience dressed as mercy still costs the disobedient."},
{q:"What judgment did the prophet pronounce on Ahab?", options:["Thy life shall go for his life, and thy people for his people","Thou shalt die in battle this year","Thy house shall serve Syria","Thy sons shall be captives"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 20:42",verse:"And he said unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Because thou hast let go out of thy hand a man whom I appointed to utter destruction, therefore thy life shall go for his life, and thy people for his people.", insight:"'Thy life shall go for his life'; sparing what God appointed to judgment puts the sentence on us."}
]}
]);
